      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### LVQ1 Results & Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "**Confusion matrix:** C2 is the most cleanly separated segment (168/173 correct),\n",
        "confirming that *Elderly Conservatives* occupy a distinct region of the feature space.\n",
        "The largest confusion is C3→C0 (36 misclassifications): *Mass Passive* and\n",
        "*Young Affluent* share moderate overlap in the prototype space, likely because\n",
        "LVQ1's single prototype per class cannot capture the internal heterogeneity of C3.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Prototype vs Medoid comparison:** the largest discrepancies are on Age\n",
        "(up to ~10 years across clusters). Medoids are real data points and may sit\n",
        "eccentrically within their cluster; LVQ1 prototypes are optimized vectors that\n",
        "converge toward the true class centroid through iterative updates, producing\n",
        "a smoother, more central representation of each segment.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Key takeaway:** the 81.4% accuracy validates that cluster boundaries are\n",
        "learnable — this prototype-based classifier recovers the segmentation structure\n",
        "with reasonable fidelity."
      ]
    },
